Description: antinomie: raise the specimen limit to 128 MiB
 The launched program's executable and an Analyze Only file are copied into
 guest memory as one immutable specimen that the host then reads in chunks.
 The copy, and the global reservation of every ready specimen, were bounded
 at 64 MiB, so a larger program was refused (EFBIG) and was not analysed.
 Raise both bounds to 128 MiB in kernel/antinomie/specimen.c: one copy of
 up to 128 MiB of guest kernel memory (vmalloc) while it waits for the host,
 released when the host has read it, or after 180 seconds idle. The copy
 keeps its 5 second limit. No other kernel file changes.
 .
 The host must not ask an older guest for more than 64 MiB (it refuses
 max_size above its own bound with EINVAL), so the larger bound is contract
 revision 19 and the control header says which revision allows which size.
Author: MikiMiku <jonathanirvinjo@gmail.com>
Origin: project
Forwarded: no
Last-Update: 2026-10-31

---
diff --git a/kernel/antinomie/control_wire.h b/kernel/antinomie/control_wire.h
index 3a0c794..d67b25d 100644
--- a/kernel/antinomie/control_wire.h
+++ b/kernel/antinomie/control_wire.h
@@ -17,7 +17,9 @@
 /* Revision 18: where reads and writes of seekable files happened, the
  * operands of in-kernel copies and allocations (file.position, file.copy), and
  * pages written through shared file mappings (lifecycle.file_mapped). */
-#define ANTC_REVISION 18
+/* Revision 19: specimens (SPECIMEN_ACQUIRE max_size and the global
+ * reservation) up to 128 MiB. */
+#define ANTC_REVISION 19
 #define ANTC_HEADER_SIZE 8
 #define ANTC_UPLOAD_BEGIN 0x1001
 #define ANTC_UPLOAD_CHUNK 0x1002
@@ -572,14 +574,16 @@
  * reserved=0 at 20, absolute path at 24, then u32 max_size, timeout_ms.
  * Acquisition reply: u64 id, u64 size, i32 status, u32 reserved=0.
  * Ready status=0 has nonzero id; unavailable negative errno has id/size=0.
- * max_size is 1..64MiB; timeout_ms is 1..5000. Initial exec captures the
+ * max_size is 1..128MiB (1..64MiB before revision 19); timeout_ms is
+ * 1..5000. Initial exec captures the
  * opened bprm file; scripts do not prove what an interpreter later reopens.
  * SPECIMEN_READ: header flags=0, u64 id at 8, u64 offset at 16,
  * u32 capacity at 24 (1..16328), u32 reserved=0 at 28. Reply: u64 offset,
  * u64 total_len, u32 count, u32 reserved=0, immutable data at 24.
  * SPECIMEN_RELEASE: header flags=0, u64 id at 8; empty reply.
  * Unknown/stale IDs rejected. Ready handles expire after 180s idle.
- * One active copy, at most four handles, 64MiB global memory reservation.
+ * One active copy, at most four handles, 128MiB global memory reservation
+ * (64MiB before revision 19).
  *
  * INPUT: header, u64 session_id at 8, bytes at 16.
  * Reply: u64 bytes_written (partial writes possible).
diff --git a/kernel/antinomie/specimen.c b/kernel/antinomie/specimen.c
index 469f54a..b8702d5 100644
--- a/kernel/antinomie/specimen.c
+++ b/kernel/antinomie/specimen.c
@@ -16,7 +16,7 @@
 #include <linux/workqueue.h>
 #include "specimen.h"
 
-#define ANT_SPECIMEN_MAX (64U * 1024 * 1024)
+#define ANT_SPECIMEN_MAX (128U * 1024 * 1024)
 #define ANT_SPECIMEN_HANDLES 4
 #define ANT_SPECIMEN_IDLE (180 * HZ)
 
